# secrets & credentials — never version
secrets/
secure-evidence/
local.json
*.token
*token*.json
*credential*
*.pem
*.key
# EXCEPTION: the rotation manifest is reference-ONLY by construction — it names
# environment variables and affected paths, and mcp_control_plane
# .validate_rotation_manifest() rejects any `value`/`secret`/`credential` key
# anywhere in it. It is a required input to validate_mcp_control_plane.py (the
# first gate sync_shared_state.ps1 runs), so `*credential*` blocking it means the
# control plane cannot be validated from a clone. The root .gitignore already
# declined to adopt `*credential*` for the same reason.
!scripts/credential_rotation_manifest.json
# EXCEPTION: the credential-forge skill directory is doctrine + tooling, not a
# secret store. Its own hygiene gate (references/hygiene.md + the skill's
# post-build validation) requires ZERO secret values on disk — names, shapes and
# paths only; values live in process memory. The blanket `*credential*` rule
# matches the skill NAME, so without this exception the dual-write projection
# (skills/credential-forge/) would land while the canonical root
# (.agents/skills/credential-forge/) silently would not — a partial projection
# that ci/check_skill_inventory_parity.py exists to catch. No file inside the
# skill carries "credential" in its basename, so the negation re-includes the
# directory only, never a stray credential file.
!skills/credential-forge/
.env
.env.*

# runtime / generated / caches
generated/
logs/
tmp/
state/
backups/
deploy-backups/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.sonar/
__pycache__/
node_modules/

# junction into ~/.claude/rules — versioned in its own home, do not duplicate
rules/
